 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "In 2007, the Swiss army invaded a country by accident.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.556
  },
  {
   "text": "170 soldiers set off on a night march through the Alps.",
   "s": 3.856,
   "e": 7.324
  },
  {
   "text": "But it was pouring rain, and the border had no fence.",
   "s": 7.624,
   "e": 10.011
  },
  {
   "text": "So they kept marching, a full mile into Liechtenstein.",
   "s": 10.311,
   "e": 12.893
  },
  {
   "text": "They carried rifles, but not one bullet.",
   "s": 13.193,
   "e": 14.885
  },
  {
   "text": "Then someone checked the map. Wrong country.",
   "s": 15.185,
   "e": 16.937
  },
  {
   "text": "So they turned around and tiptoed back to Switzerland.",
   "s": 17.237,
   "e": 19.541
  },
  {
   "text": "But here's the part nobody saw coming: Liechtenstein has no army.",
   "s": 19.841,
   "e": 23.366
  },
  {
   "text": "Nobody there even noticed the invasion.",
   "s": 23.666,
   "e": 25.237
  },
  {
   "text": "A spokeswoman shrugged off the Swiss army: \"It has happened before.\"",
   "s": 25.537,
   "e": 28.695
  }
 ],
